# Template for release signing configuration. No secret values belong in Git.
#
# The keystore and the inline passwords that used to live in build.gradle and in
# ../robloxAndroidPK_DO_NOT_DELETE were published with this repository. Treat that
# key as compromised, rotate it, and never re-commit it.
#
# Release builds read these values from environment variables (set them from a
# protected CI secret store, or from an untracked local shell profile):
#
#   ROBLOX_RELEASE_KEYSTORE        absolute path to the NEW .jks/.keystore file
#   ROBLOX_RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD  keystore password
#   ROBLOX_RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS       key alias inside the keystore
#   ROBLOX_RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD    key password
#
# If any of them is missing, the release build is produced unsigned instead of
# silently falling back to the exposed key.
#
# Fabric/Crashlytics release uploads additionally need a rotated apiSecret;
# inject it into crashlytics.properties from CI (see that file's comments).
#
# Machine-local SDK/NDK locations go into an untracked local.properties:
#
#   sdk.dir=/path/to/Android/sdk
#   ndk.dir=/path/to/Android/ndk
#
# and ANDROID_NDK_HOME (or ndk-build on PATH) is used for the native build.
